3.1
user came to log in application , and we want to send welcome email
POST/singup {fname,lname,email} -> storing it in database
sendEmail() ---------> return success (but this is synchronous)  (third-party apis is called)

problem :- latency because of external system.
           system depends on external service.
           rate limiting issues because third parties impose rate limit. (let's suppose 100 people are pressing sign-up button at the same time.)

3.2
(i) Addition of email server

now , sync causing the problem , so make it async.
when post api call , store the data in a database (workflow as same as above) , but add another
server which will handle emails .
email server , will sendReqToEmailServer
email server will maintain the connection with gmail.

but still 30 calls - OK , 70 calls - FAIL (but possibility of crashing reduced)

(ii) Introduce queue
-> enqueue :- sendReqToQueue , not waiting for the request to be processed => reducing latency
-> if , the request is not processed, re-add it in queue. => retry
   if the service is down for one day , then it will re-add continuoulsy wasting the operations.
   so for this introducing exponential back-off mechanism. 
   0 seconds -> 1 -> 2 -> 4 -> 8 -> 16
   and max Retry can also be introduced. like if max Retry is reached , then the request can be added in
   dead letter queue. which can be monitored by user manually.
   
-> if rate limiting 35 messages/second , only allowing 25 messages/second => rate limiting also handled
                              by introducing delay after sending 25 messages per second.

(iii) Load balancer
     distributes the load evenly among the users.

-> one server which watches the queue and then sends the email accordingly to the third party apis.
workflow :- users -> load balancer -> queue 

