(iii) 
http connection :- client sends the request , and the server only sends the ack or response. and use get for getting the messages
                    but simple unnecessary calls , because what if user has not seen the message.
long polling :- client sends the request to the server , and waits for the response from the server.
server sent event (SSE) :- here , the server sends the response to the registered client , unidirectional
web socket connection :- full duplex connection between client and server and sent in real time,
                          no delay or wait.


5.4.2
Chat Service Layer
user ->  load balancer +  gateway -> various chat servers

so, dedicated websocket gateway + load balancer for various chat services.

so, when one user wants to chat with another user ,
websocket connection needs to established between both of them.

so, the user is sending message to his friend containing (message,to,from)
and users are connected to different chat servers.
so, there should be mapping between userId and the chat server. => this is present in redis cache.
this is websocket registry. 
websocket connection is very heavy weight and has very high bandwidth. so , it is not possible to open up
for 1 billion websocket connection over here. so TTL will be present over here. so, web socket connection 
will get deleted from web socket registry.

now , it may happen , that one user is not able to send the message to another user because user is offline.
so this data needs to be stored in the database.(chatDB (cassandra or dynamo db) or groupDB)

chatDB -> id , chatId , messageId , senderId,receiverId , message , type (text/image) , timestamp , deliveryStatus

